<Project>
  <!--
    Repo-wide NuGet version overrides to patch transitive dependency CVEs.

    Scriban: PINNED TO 6.x ON PURPOSE — DO NOT BUMP TO 7.x.
    Volo.Abp.TextTemplating.Scriban 10.0.2 is compiled against Scriban 6.x, where
    Scriban.Parsing.ParserOptions is a different kind of type than in 7.x. Loading 7.x
    at runtime throws
        System.TypeLoadException: Could not load type 'Scriban.Parsing.ParserOptions'
        from assembly 'Volo.Abp.TextTemplating.Scriban' due to value type mismatch
    inside ScribanTemplateRenderingEngine, i.e. EVERY ABP text template fails to render:
    the forgot-password reset email, the email-confirmation mail, etc. The account pages
    return 500 and no mail is ever sent.
    Build + unit tests do NOT catch this (same trap as the AutoMapper note below);
    only an actual template render does — verified 2026-08-26 by POSTing
    /Account/ForgotPassword: 7.2.2 -> TypeLoadException, 6.6.0 -> 302 + mail rendered.
    The earlier "ABP 10.4.0 already moved to Scriban >= 7.0.0, confirming 7.x is
    API-compatible" reasoning was wrong for THIS ABP version: 10.4 ships a Scriban 7
    build, 10.0.2 does not.

    Trade-off accepted: 6.6.0 leaves GHSA-5wr9-m6jw-xx44 (critical) and
    GHSA-24c8-4792-22hx (high) open. Both are attacks through malicious *template
    content*, which is unreachable here: this solution has no Volo.Abp.TextTemplating
    package reference of its own and no TextTemplateManagement module, so nobody —
    tenant admin included — can author or edit a template. Only ABP's built-in static
    templates are rendered, with model data escaped by Scriban as values, not code.
    Revisit when ABP is upgraded to >= 10.4: then move back to Scriban 7.2.2+.

    AutoMapper: Volo.Abp.AutoMapper 10.0.2 ships AutoMapper 14.0.0 (GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x / CVE-2026-32933).
    DO NOT bump to 15.x: AutoMapper 15 changed the MapperConfiguration ctor
    (removed MapperConfiguration(MapperConfigurationExpression)), which ABP 10.0.2
    calls — causing MissingMethodException at runtime container resolution so EVERY
    AutoMapper-backed /api/app/* returns 500. Build + unit tests do NOT catch this;
    only a live authenticated API call does (verified 2026-06-08 on main a845805).
    Stay on 14.0.0 until ABP is upgraded to a build compiled against AutoMapper 15.x.
    Trade-off: CVE-2026-32933 stays open in dev (no 14.x fix exists).

  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Scriban" Version="6.6.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="AutoMapper" Version="14.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
